  title: "The Atlantic Gateway: Where Europe First Met the Northeast",
  description: "The Gulf of St. Lawrence and the coasts around it were the first part of Canada that Europeans reached and the last part of it that most Canadian histories visit. This lesson follows the fishermen, whalers, colonists, missionaries and surveyors from Cabot to Bayfield, and the Mi'kmaq, Beothuk, Innu and Inuit whose coasts they came to, asking what kind of history a coast makes when the ships come every summer and go home every fall.",
  gradeLevel: "7-9", topic: "Exploration", estimatedMinutes: 75, readingTimeMinutes: 12,
